<!-- CORE FEATURES -->
<section class="gate-section" id="features">
  <div class="gate-container-wide">
    <p class="section-label reveal">Core features</p>
    <div class="gate-features-grid reveal" style="transition-delay: 0.05s;">
      <div class="gate-feature-card">
        <h3>{{ versions.gate.rules }} Detection Rules</h3>
        <p>Bundled patterns for cloud, source-control, payment, AI, database, and private-key credential shapes. The rule count is generated from the current catalog; coverage is not a guarantee.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="gate-feature-card">
        <h3>Credential Verification</h3>
        <p>Opt-in <code>--verify</code> sends the credential to a provider adapter. “Inactive” currently lowers severity, so read the adapter and threshold caveats before enabling it.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="gate-feature-card">
        <h3>Bounded source rewrites</h3>
        <p>Can move selected hardcoded-string patterns into an environment file and rewrite bounded source forms. It is textual, not semantic, and has documented conflict and language gaps.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="gate-feature-card">
        <h3>Interactive Remediation</h3>
        <p>Walk through findings to fix, vault, ignore, skip, or open guidance. Vault references have no application runtime resolver, and ignores are policy bypasses.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="gate-feature-card">
        <h3>Incident artifacts</h3>
        <p>Prints rotation/audit guidance and creates purge and incident-record artifacts. It does not rotate, investigate, fix, execute a purge, or update completion state.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="gate-feature-card">
        <h3>Reports with framework labels</h3>
        <p>Summarizes the current local audit log and attaches static OWASP 2021, NIST SP 800-53, CIS Controls, and SOC 2 labels. It is not an attestation.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="gate-feature-card">
        <h3>SARIF Output</h3>
        <p>Emits SARIF 2.1.0. The GitHub Action can attempt an upload when token permissions and repository support allow it.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="gate-feature-card">
        <h3>Git History Scanning</h3>
        <p>Scans past commits for secrets and generates purge scripts you can review and run to rewrite history.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="gate-feature-card">
        <h3>Works without a config file</h3>
        <p>Runs on defaults. No setup file, account, or API key required to start; add a <code>.gaterc</code> when you need one.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- GITHUB ACTION -->
<section class="gate-section" id="docs-github-action">
  <div class="gate-container-wide">
    <p class="section-label reveal">CI/CD</p>
    <div class="gate-docs-section reveal">
      <h2 class="gate-docs-heading">GitHub Action</h2>
      <p class="gate-docs-text">The action defaults to report/warn, installs the unversioned npm CLI when Gate is absent, and only attempts SARIF upload when requested. Pin the CLI separately and choose blocking behavior explicitly.</p>

      <div class="gate-gh-action">
        <div class="gate-gh-action-bar">.github/workflows/gate.yml</div>
        <div class="gate-gh-action-body"><span class="kw">name</span>: Gate
<span class="kw">on</span>: [pull_request, push]

<span class="kw">permissions</span>:
  <span class="kw">contents</span>: read
  <span class="kw">pull-requests</span>: write
  <span class="kw">security-events</span>: write

<span class="kw">jobs</span>:
  <span class="kw">scan</span>:
    <span class="kw">runs-on</span>: ubuntu-latest
    <span class="kw">steps</span>:
      - <span class="kw">uses</span>: actions/checkout@v4
      - <span class="kw">run</span>: npm install -g @penumbraforge/gate@{{ versions.gate.version }}
      - <span class="kw">uses</span>: penumbraforge/gate@v2
        <span class="kw">with</span>:
          <span class="kw">mode</span>: enforce
          <span class="kw">verify</span>: <span class="val">false</span>
          <span class="kw">format</span>: sarif
          <span class="kw">fail-on</span>: high</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

