<!-- SECURITY PROMISE -->
<section class="gate-section" id="security">
  <div class="gate-container">
    <p class="section-label reveal">How Gate handles your data</p>
    <div class="gate-security-list reveal" style="transition-delay: 0.05s;">
      <div class="gate-security-item"><strong>Local default scan.</strong> Gate has no intentional product telemetry. Opt-in <code>--verify</code> sends a credential to its provider, and update operations can also use the network.</div>
      <div class="gate-security-item"><strong>Secret-bearing local state.</strong> Gate requests restrictive modes for sensitive files, but snapshots can contain plaintext and the current audit writer can retain a raw <code>secret</code> field.</div>
      <div class="gate-security-item"><strong>Scoped atomic rewrites.</strong> Core source-file fixes use a temporary file and rename. Not every config, state, vault, or report write shares that boundary.</div>
      <div class="gate-security-item"><strong>Redacted supported outputs.</strong> Review machine formats, debug output, and generated artifacts before sharing them.</div>
      <div class="gate-security-item"><strong>TLS for verification.</strong> Provider API calls during <code>--verify</code> go over TLS.</div>
      <div class="gate-security-item"><strong>Hook mismatch.</strong> Generated hooks and the CLI currently use different environment-variable names for pre-commit behavior; keep config verification off and inspect staging after fixes.</div>
      <div class="gate-security-item"><strong>Mixed subprocess paths.</strong> Some paths use explicit argument arrays; other current paths invoke shell-backed commands. Treat repository paths and generated commands as untrusted until reviewed.</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<script>
  // Reveal animations come from the shared handler in base.njk.
  document.querySelectorAll('.gate-copy-btn[data-copy]').forEach(function(btn) {
    btn.addEventListener('click', function() {
      navigator.clipboard.writeText(btn.dataset.copy).then(function() {
        btn.textContent = 'copied';
        btn.classList.add('copied');
        setTimeout(function() {
          btn.textContent = 'copy';
          btn.classList.remove('copied');
        }, 2000);
      });
    });
  });
</script>
